WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:05.630
It's Wednesday, and this is the Microsoft for Education Daily.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:09.510
Let's catch you up on everything new from Microsoft.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:17.610
Your call: without a Copilot licence,

00:00:17.610 --> 00:00:22.000
search in the Microsoft 365 Copilot app is getting a refresh.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:27.350
It's on by default, with a switch back to classic search, The Register reports.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:34.290
Locking Copilot Chat to Study and Learn?

00:00:34.290 --> 00:00:37.850
Microsoft's new how-to says the lock is for students only.

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:41.130
Teachers keep their Copilot,

00:00:41.130 --> 00:00:45.330
while students get Study and Learn in Edge, Teams and Outlook too.

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:46.930
Big town hall?

00:00:46.930 --> 00:00:51.870
Teams events for up to 100,000 people get raised hands, due December.

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:56.440
Organizers can let a raised hand turn on their mic and camera,

00:00:56.440 --> 00:00:58.530
and everyone can send reactions.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:03.220
School IT can now set maintenance windows in Intune,

00:01:03.220 --> 00:01:06.380
so automatic updates only start in hours you pick.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:11.450
Microsoft suggests it for kiosks and critical devices,

00:01:11.450 --> 00:01:14.220
on Windows 11, version 24H2 or later.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:18.860
Teams will flag likely scams on calls from outside your organization,

00:01:18.860 --> 00:01:20.640
with a preview due in December.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:24.420
Student team project on GitHub?

00:01:24.420 --> 00:01:28.750
Issues now get statuses and a drag-and-drop board, in public preview.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:34.320
Teaching from a Mac? PowerPoint's Presenter view will let you move,

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:37.150
resize and enlarge your notes, due January.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:40.720
And Outlook's follow-up flags will take your own words,

00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:42.770
so you remember why, due February.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:50.300
The fine print? Attackers stole secrets via an Azure API Management flaw.

00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:52.110
It's fixed; rotate them.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:55.770
And Windows deprecated its Family Safety app and Bluet

00:01:55.770 --> 00:01:59.050
ooth file transfers; the phone app and USB still work.

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:05.950
After hours, Edge will let you pick a profile when it starts,

00:02:05.950 --> 00:02:08.560
work, personal or guest, due February.

00:02:09.380 --> 00:02:12.620
And flight-sim fans can now fly the Global Jet,

00:02:12.620 --> 00:02:15.370
a new add-on for Flight Simulator 2024.

00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:22.180
It's a business jet with a head-up display and a range of 6,000 nautical miles.

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:28.360
Search, updates, profiles, even who speaks next: more of it is your call.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.350
Zoom out, and it never stops shipping.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.800
Check the board: shipped today, and more on the way.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:40.690
All of that, in one day. And it keeps on shipping.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.870
You've been watching the Microsoft for Education Daily.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:51.340
Go build something. See you tomorrow.
